(i) Demolish 85.4sqm, including non-original additions to the existing house and a detached shed;
(ii) Renovate the existing protected Maryville House (RPS No. 463);
(iii) Constructi two 4-storey residential blocks located to the northeast and southwest of Maryville House connected to the House by single-storey glazed links;
(iv) Create 32 no. two-bed apartments, comprising 14 units in Block A, 14 units in Block B and 4 units in Maryville House, served by 673sqm of communal open space. All apartments have private terraces.
The development features 90 no. bicycle spaces (16 visitor spaces and 74 resident spaces); 20 no. car parking spaces; refuse storage; landscaping; foul and surface water drainage and all associated site development works.

